From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:02:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Declare the DirectX 6 Direct3D immediate-mode interfaces in
 miniwin

Add IDirect3D3, IDirect3DDevice3, IDirect3DViewport3 (over a new
IDirect3DViewport), IDirect3DTexture2 and IDirect3DMaterial3, with
their IIDs and the D3DMATRIX, D3DRECT, D3DMATERIAL and state-type
declarations their methods take.

The interfaces are answered by existing objects where the DirectX
object model allows it:
- DirectDrawImpl implements IDirect3D3 (QueryInterface IID_IDirect3D3).
- Direct3DRMRenderer, the object miniwin hands out as IDirect3DDevice2,
  implements IDirect3DDevice3 and answers IID_IDirect3DDevice2 and
  IID_IDirect3DDevice3.
- DirectDrawSurfaceImpl implements IDirect3DTexture2, as a DirectDraw
  surface does.

IDirect3DMaterial3 and IDirect3DViewport3 get new stub classes;
IDirect3D3::CreateMaterial creates the material. Every new method
logs once and returns DDERR_UNSUPPORTED.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

